# Paranal Airglow Line And Continuum Emission (PALACE) model: data and code of
# v1.0 (Noll et al. 2024)
#
# Reference populations and intensities from the OH population model for lines
# with HITRAN2020 data (intensities consistent with pmd_reflineint_mol.dat)
#
# Column names:
# lam: vacuum wavelength in µm (HITRAN2020)
# ID: 13 characters describing upper and lower states (HITRAN2020)
# (see pmd_reflineint_mol.dat for details)
# vi: vibrational level of upper state
# Fi: electronic substate of upper state (1 or 2)
# Ni: rotational level of upper state
# pi: parity of upper state (e or f)
# Ei: energy of upper state in 1/cm (HITRAN2020)
# Aij: Einstein-A coefficient in 1/s (HITRAN2020)
# Aijc: corrected Einstein-A coefficient in 1/s (see pmd_corrA_Ohbands.dat
# for branch and band corrections and noll+20 for Lambda doublets)
# gi: statistical weight (HITRAN2020)
# y: natural logarithm of population (exp(y) in Rs)
# I: reference intensity in R (based on product of exp(y), Aijc, and gi)
#
# References:
# HITRAN2020: https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jqsrt.2021.107949
# noll+20: https://doi.org/10.5194/acp-20-5269-2020
#
#
# lvmsky empirical OH coefficients for Skyfar-response calibration.
# Parent PALACE table: pmd_popmodel_OH_telluric_upper_parity_lsf_adam_25000_v1.dat
# Run fingerprint: a53af79abce4efaf70f7faa036ab6b16049d8b015227e5656c5e835ac1243d2b
# Calibration: fixed-baseline linear weighted SSE with VNF q-closure; ridge lambda=0.1.
# Corpus: 12857 FLUX_SKY_FAR spectra; MJD-disjoint train/validation/holdout.
# Mapping: 22058 rows; only Aijc and I changed; sum(Aijc * gi) preserved per (vi, Ni, Fi) VNF group.
